<div id="FilteringStringText" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="1235" data-tchmi-height="48" data-tchmi-width="528">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold;">4. The same filter as a string</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px;">String syntax uses <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">||</code>, <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">&amp;&amp;</code> and brackets.</p>
</div>
<div id="FilteringStringCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="1291" data-tchmi-height="75" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">filter:
    'properties::hasUppercase == true <span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">||</span> ' +
    '<span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">(</span>properties::chars[1] == "o" <span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">&amp;&amp;</span> properties::length &gt;= 6<span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">)</span>',</pre>
</div>
